# evidence-for: NFR-002, FR-020, AC-025
# evidence-volatile: \d+\.\d+s
# evidence-volatile: Installed \d+ packages in \d+ms
# evidence-timeout: 300
#
# D-137 — THE READ AND THE DECODE ARE ONE OPERATION.
#
# Fourteen sites across seven modules (the ledger found thirteen; the AST scan
# below found `scripts/validate_intent_coverage.py:616` too) wrote
#
#     json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
#
# under a handler naming `json.JSONDecodeError` — nine of them adding OSError.
# None of those handlers catch what `read_text` itself raises. UnicodeDecodeError
# is a subclass of ValueError and NOT of JSONDecodeError, and it is raised BEFORE
# json.loads is ever reached. So one non-UTF-8 byte in castings/manifest.json
# raised straight across the MCP boundary from both spawn doors — the exact doors
# the previous cycle had hardened for JSON-shape corruption.
#
# THE STRUCTURAL HALF, which is why this is the escalated class rather than a
# bug: `test_no_document_load_can_raise_across_the_mcp_boundary` COUNTED ALL
# FOURTEEN AS GUARDED. It matched handler names against
#
#     _DECODE_HANDLER_NAMES = {"ValueError", "JSONDecodeError", "Exception",
#                              "BaseException"}
#
# a hand-kept frozenset someone typed. A guard whose own membership table is
# hand-kept is an instance of the class it exists to make unrepresentable, and
# its failure mode is SILENT ACCEPTANCE — the worst direction.
#
# THE FIX, on both axes:
#
#   MEMBERS   — one guarded primitive, `foundry_state.read_json` /
#               `read_document` / `read_text_file`, in the package's LEAF module:
#               the one thing both foundry.py and foundry_orchestrator.py already
#               import, so every module can reach it with no risk of closing a
#               cycle in the import graph. That cycle risk is the whole reason
#               the two tolerant loaders were separate copies to begin with.
#               All fourteen sites now call it, plus forge_spec.py:426
#               (D-140's residual, swept here because it is the same class).
#
#   THE RULE  — coverage is no longer a name match. What the expression RAISES is
#               computed from the expression; what a handler CATCHES is resolved
#               to a real exception class through the module's own namespace and
#               asked `issubclass`. Python decides, not a list. An unresolvable
#               handler name covers nothing (the conservative direction) and is
#               REPORTED in the offender line, so an unrecognised member
#               announces itself instead of quietly widening the gap.
#
# The two `_read_document` bodies are now one: this module's is the canonical
# primitive and foundry_orchestrator's is an import of it. foundry.py keeps its
# own body because THIS module imports THAT one — and it PASSES the narrowed rule
# on its own merits, which is the only reason it is allowed to stay. There is no
# allow-list to add anything to.
#
# WHAT WAS RED BEFORE THE FIX (the scan, run against the unfixed tree):
#   evidence.py:1287,1317 · foundry_orchestrator.py:1422,4251 ·
#   foundry_spawn.py:616,640,1285,1468,1575 · foundry_validate.py:60 ·
#   intent_coverage.py:248,400 · scripts/validate_intent_coverage.py:369,616
#   = 14 sites, 7 modules. The scan reported ZERO of them.
#
# The `-- control --` block is what keeps the refusal narrow: the same document
# as valid UTF-8 still spawns. A rule that reported every document load would
# have forced the canonical primitive into an allow-list, which is the mechanism
# this replaces.
== D-137: one non-UTF-8 byte in castings/manifest.json ==

-- why `except json.JSONDecodeError` never covered this --
   issubclass(UnicodeDecodeError, ValueError)           = True
   issubclass(UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError) = False
   the 14-site shape  : RAISES UnicodeDecodeError

-- the same byte through the shipped doors, post-fix --
   Foundry-Spawn-Teammate   ok=False  names the file=True
      manifest.json could not be read (UnicodeDecodeError: 'utf-8' codec can't decode byte 0xe9 in position 59: invalid continuation byte)
   Foundry-Cast-Wave        ok=False  names the file=True
      manifest.json could not be read (UnicodeDecodeError: 'utf-8' codec can't decode byte 0xe9 in position 59: invalid continuation byte)
   both doors tell ONE story about the file: True

-- control: the refusal is NARROW (same document, valid UTF-8) --
   Foundry-Spawn-Teammate   ok=True  read-fault reported=False
   Foundry-Cast-Wave        ok=True  read-fault reported=False

